    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 334\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 7966-C, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to the amount of the\n      supplemental basic tuition for charter schools\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  require  the  State  to  reimburse school districts\noutside of New York City for supplemental basic tuition payments made to\ncharter schools in the same school year as the district's  payments  are\nmade, beginning with the 2018-19 school year.\n \n  These  payments  are  currently  made  to school districts in the year\nfollowing the district's expense, based  upon  the  prior  year's  final\nreconciled  expenses.  Making payment in the following year is necessary\nso that the state payment amount reflects  an  actual  final  enrollment\ncount.  Making  the  payment in the current year would require use of an\nestimated enrollment and would need to be reconciled after  the  payment\nis  made,  resulting  in overlapping claims or recoveries and increasing\npotential for accounting errors.\n \n  Further, this topic was discussed in the context of the 2018-19 budget\nprocess, but ultimately was not included in the  final  enacted  budget.\nThe bill would create a $30 million financial obligation to the state in\nthe  current year outside of the budget process, and would not adhere to\nthe 2019 enacted budget agreement.  For  the  foregoing  reasons,  I  am\nconstrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 334,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2018
   }
